   "Send this to your study partner before the practical."
  ],
  "grid_title": "PLANES OF THE BODY",
  "why": "All from anatomical position. Sagittal plane: divides the body vertically into right and left (sagitta is Latin for arrow); down the exact middle it's the midsagittal (median) plane, off-center it's parasagittal. Flexion and extension (nodding yes) happen in the sagittal plane. Frontal (coronal) plane: divides the body into front (anterior) and back (posterior); corona is Latin for crown. Abduction and adduction (jumping jacks) happen in the frontal plane. Transverse (axial) plane: divides the body horizontally into upper and lower parts; scans show it as cross sections. Rotation (shaking your head no, at the joint between C1 and C2) happens in the transverse plane.",
